{"authorDailyContributionsMap":{"yhthia":[{"date":"2025-11-01T00:00:00","commitResults":[{"hash":"249587a1b8186710007e55f48739e93a28bc4e77","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Improve same person validation","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":6,"deletions":4},"test-code":{"insertions":8,"deletions":20}}},{"hash":"55d192db6b2f0ad2497797c3ea303d3f39b22482","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Store email as lowercase","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":1,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"d4c93713dc62e470d090757f47c6c846c51759bf","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Improve date validation","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":3,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"13763e2135794b11b6d0d9583edd9c2f85d0c9d9","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Improve name validation","messageBody":"The parser finds all known prefixes in an input string even when a\nprefix is inside the value of another field. This prevents users from\nentering names with text resembling a prefix and creates a poor user\nexperience. Moreover, only alphanumerical characters are allowed which\nis overly restrictive for certain names that contain hyphens or\napostrophes.\n\nLet\u0027s:\n* expand the regex to allow Unicode and a set of special\nnon-alphanumerical characters that are commonly found in names\n* allow users to enclose names with prefixes with one set of double\nquotes\n* capitalize letters following any of these new special characters for\nbetter formatting\n\nMaking the tokenizer quote-aware is the most robust solution to this\nproblem, because it allows the Name field to be fully flexible without\nrequiring users to avoid certain characters.\n\nA small side effect that results from this consistent naming standard\nis that names with multiple capitalised letters will only have their\nfirst letter capitalised.\n","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":45,"deletions":18},"docs":{"insertions":10,"deletions":1},"test-code":{"insertions":42,"deletions":7}}},{"hash":"8cf55fa766e97a734164f623082dfb576857cc0f","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Improve phone number validation","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":2,"deletions":2},"test-code":{"insertions":9,"deletions":9}}},{"hash":"bf4e0c0a6bacc461ad7fdb82d4a7d84dbe669a97","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix missing MS error message","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":4,"deletions":0}}},{"hash":"7dfb760db934979daff8abaf71ca6c424e58a4c2","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add dependents upper bound","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":5,"deletions":3}}},{"hash":"e65a7fa237a1fae9e74679214badc3379bf9d73c","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Fix Salary rounding error","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":2,"deletions":1}}},{"hash":"9b4f3c1173c37a682a8343a5741509d813e62971","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Make tags case insensitive","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":2,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"67a86654dc99394b243f354ff51552194b57b58a","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Update duplicate person error messages","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":2,"deletions":2},"test-code":{"insertions":2,"deletions":2}}},{"hash":"0db0bd3bd6f82b67eb66def49317f771cc7c9da7","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Shorten edit person success message","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"functional-code":{"insertions":54,"deletions":15},"test-code":{"insertions":13,"deletions":6}}},{"hash":"164a6e31b8a351a422142dd83f0241fb0eb390ff","isMergeCommit":false,"messageTitle":"Add input parameter constraints to UG","messageBody":"","fileTypesAndContributionMap":{"docs":{"insertions":59,"deletions":8}}},{"hash":"